course: dictionary
lesson: 10030
title: A tent, and the words around it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A tent is a shelter made of cloth or nylon, held up by poles and ropes. You put one up when you go camping. Sometimes a word has more than one meaning, so the words around it show you which meaning fits.
explain: «Never use a stove, heater or barbecue inside a tent, because of fire and carbon monoxide, a poison gas you cannot smell.» The sentence tells you a tent is a place where people sleep, so a fire inside it would be dangerous. Read the clues, not just the word.
explain: «The kea is a clever, curious mountain parrot from New Zealand, famous for pulling apart cars, bags and tents.» Here the tent is something a bird can tear apart, so you can picture it as cloth. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: A big tent is different. It can be used for a circus or a party, and then it is sometimes called a marquee. The word is the same, but the clues show which kind of tent is meant.
fact: A tent is a shelter made of cloth or nylon, held up by poles and ropes.
fact: You put up a tent when you go camping, and you take it down when you pack up.
fact: A big tent is used for a circus or a party, and it is also called a marquee.
fact: Carbon monoxide is a poison gas you cannot smell, so never use a stove, heater or barbecue inside a tent.
fact: In maths, tents can be counted: if 21 people need tents that hold 4 each, you need 6 tents, because you must round up.
exercise: «Never use a stove, heater or barbecue inside a tent.» Why is this rule given? | To keep the tent warm for sleeping | To stop the tent from floating away | *Because of fire and carbon monoxide, a poison gas you cannot smell | So the tent can be taken down quickly
exercise: Twenty-one children go camping, and each tent holds four children. How many tents are needed? | 4 | 21 | *6 | 5
exercise: «The kea is a clever, curious mountain parrot from New Zealand, famous for pulling apart cars, bags and tents.» What does this tell you about the tent? | It is a poison gas | *It is made of cloth or nylon that a bird can tear apart | It is a big shelter for a circus | It is a kind of mountain made of stone
test: What is a tent? | A poison gas you cannot smell | A type of mountain parrot | *A shelter of cloth or nylon, held up by poles and ropes | A big metal box for food
test: «They keep all food in a bear-proof container away from the tents.» Where should all food be kept? | Inside the tent, next to the sleeping bags | In the pockets of your coat | Next to the stove | *In a bear-proof container away from the tents
exam: Which is the best safety rule for camping? | *Never bring a stove, heater or barbecue into a tent | Always light a fire inside the tent to keep warm | Take snacks into the tent to eat at night | Put the tent up on the edge of a steep drop
